In article <CKBEoy.EuF@mcm.hp.com>, marco@hpmcaa.mcm.hp.com (Marco Dalla-Gasperina) writes:
>Hey Experts...
>
>I've noticed that when I'm in mine town and I'm lucky enough to
>have a temple to my god on that level... all the monsters basically
>run away from me.  They may hit me near the general store but if I
>try to lure them closer they drift away.  Is this intentional?  If it
>is, it's a great idea and infuriating as hell!

If it's a co-aligned temple with a priest, then it's supposed to be
a sanctuary for you.  No monsters will enter it while you're in it.
If you leave, they might enter, and then maybe you could run in and 
kill them.  This might not be as hard as it sounds if you have a pick
axe/wand of digging


----|-----
|        |
|        |
|   _    |
----|-----
    @

You might be able make a little build a little closet and wait for
monsters there.  (I think this would work, but haven't tried).
Otherwise just use a wand of create monster in the temple.
>
>On a related note... what are the odds of a monster leaving a corpse?
>It seems that on a level with an aligned alter, the odds go down.  Some
>monsters (like grid bugs) don't leave corpses.  One especially good game
>I killed about 30 Wraiths and none left a corpse (I was trying to make
>my quest experience level, but never got to it).
>
>marco

Let's peek at the code:

                if (bigmonst(mdat) || mdat == &mons[PM_LIZARD]
                           || is_golem(mdat)
                           || is_mplayer(mdat)
                           || is_rider(mdat))
                        chance = 1;
                else chance = !rn2((int)
                        (2 + ((mdat->geno & G_FREQ)<2) + verysmall(mdat)));
                if (chance)
                        (void) make_corpse(mtmp);

I'm not really sure what all those flags are (what G_FREQ is) but it looks
to me like it's between always between 1/2 and 1/4.  make_corpse probably
changes the odds in certain circumstatnes (ie: grid bugs never make corpses),

For wraiths, I don't believe there are any special conditions, the odds
should be 1/2 leave corpses.  My quick test in wizard mode seems to
confirm those odds.   Not to seem insulting, but are you sure that you
didn't have a blindfold on when you killed those 30 wraiths, and just
didn't notice that 15 (or so) of them had left corpses?
 
